From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:32:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bluez5: modemmanager: number calls from 1 in +CLCC

The native HFP AG answered AT+CLCC with call index 0: modemmanager.c
never set call->index, and calloc left it at 0. 3GPP TS 27.007 numbers
calls from 1, and a car kit that polls AT+CLCC drops a call with index
0: no call on its display and no audio either way, although the SCO
link stands. Give each new call the lowest free index from 1, as a
modem does.

Found and confirmed in a car by furios_audio (FuriOS on a Volla phone).
---
 spa/plugins/bluez5/modemmanager.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spa/plugins/bluez5/modemmanager.c b/spa/plugins/bluez5/modemmanager.c
index a01e575..b1003cc 100644
--- a/spa/plugins/bluez5/modemmanager.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/bluez5/modemmanager.c
@@ -457,6 +457,23 @@ static bool mm_get_managed_objects(struct impl *this)
 	return true;
 }
 
+static unsigned int mm_next_call_index(struct impl *this)
+{
+	/* 3GPP TS 27.007 +CLCC: call identification numbers start at 1. Reuse the
+	 * lowest free one, like a modem does. */
+	unsigned int index = 1;
+	struct call *call;
+
+again:
+	spa_list_for_each(call, &this->call_list, link) {
+		if (call->index == index) {
+			index++;
+			goto again;
+		}
+	}
+	return index;
+}
+
 static void call_free(struct call *call)
 {
 	spa_list_remove(&call->link);
@@ -641,6 +658,7 @@ static DBusHandlerResult mm_filter_cb(DBusConnection *bus, DBusMessage *m, void
 			free(call_object);
 			return DBUS_HANDLER_RESULT_NEED_MEMORY;
 		}
+		call_object->index = mm_next_call_index(this);
 		spa_list_append(&this->call_list, &call_object->link);
 
 		m2 = dbus_message_new_method_call(MM_DBUS_SERVICE, path, DBUS_INTERFACE_PROPERTIES, "GetAll");
